From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:25:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 278/289] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on reviewer
 personas (0278)

Review round 1 of the persona work (patch 0277).

Lead notice (omnigent/inner/ae_reviewers.py):
- The lead-picks line for a persona that runs only when risky now carries the
  persona's trigger, so the lead can tell whether the diff qualifies.
- A persona's instructions keep their indentation and blank lines when quoted
  for the lead to copy; a blank line is a lone ">".
- A persona's name, purpose and trigger are put in quotation marks, and
  bidi-override, zero-width and other invisible characters are removed, so
  user text cannot read as the notice's own sentence.

Web:
- The per-session "Who works on this?" dialog now passes the persona catalog
  to the reviewer rows, so Customize shows persona slots as they are.
- Removing reviewer 1 no longer leaves a persona that runs only when risky in
  slot 1: the persona is dropped from the promoted slot, which keeps the model
  and effort it showed, and a status note says so.
- Deleting a persona writes its model and effort into the slots that named it
  (saved presets and unsaved drafts alike), so every preset stays valid; the
  dialog text says what happens and counts unsaved drafts.
- One malformed stored persona is skipped on its own instead of dropping the
  whole list.
- A tab is allowed in instructions; every refused character is named plainly,
  and invisible or direction-changing characters are refused.
- The 20-persona cap reason is visible text tied to the disabled buttons, the
  missing-persona note is tied to its select, and the form's problems sit in
  a live region.
